[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/Therapy room.png" fade="0.0"]
set {flags.intro_done} = true
audio mbg1 "res://assets/audio/ElevenLabs_Cosy_therapist_office,_ full.mp3"
audio mbg2 "res://assets/audio/Silent clock ticking.mp3" [volume="-4.0"]
narrator: The office smells of fresh paint, someone else's furniture polish, and whatever decision made the last occupant leave in a hurry.
narrator: The desk is mahogany. Real mahogany. Expensive taste for a man who apparently vanished on a Tuesday.
player: [i]The ink on my license is six weeks old. The filing cabinet is empty. The lease is paid through March. This is either the beginning of something or the evidence of it.[/i]
narrator: The door hits the frame hard enough to rattle the frosted glass. A beat of silence. Then the handle moves.
audio "res://assets/audio/Door sound - Entering the room.mp3"
narrator: A young woman enters sideways, balancing a clipboard, a box of folders, and a coffee that has already lost the structural argument. She deposits the box on the desk with both intention and consequence.
join bea leftmost
bea: I'm fine. Nobody needed to see that, and nobody did.
narrator: She straightens her glasses. A sticky note migrates from the box to her forearm without her noticing. She looks at you with the focused assessment of someone who has done this before and is deciding whether to do it again.
bea: Good morning. I'm Beatrix. You'll call me Bea. I came with the lease.
player: Morning. I gathered. What exactly did you come with?
bea: Everything that survived the previous arrangement. The client licenses, the appointment calendar, the good coffee machine he didn't think to take because he left in something of a hurry. I kept everything running for three weeks while the management company found you.
player: [i]Three weeks. She ran this practice alone and didn't say it like a complaint.[/i]
narrator: She opens the folder on the clipboard with the efficiency of someone who has already organized the morning in her head and is now executing it from memory.
bea: He left a few things I didn't know what to do with.
player: Like what?
bea: The filing cabinet is cleared out. Most of the books are gone. There's a door at the back that was locked when he left and I haven't found the key. I haven't looked very hard.
narrator: She says this last part to the clipboard.
# CH_INTRO_01 | OPT_01=Clinical [composure:easy]  OPT_02=Filed [default]  OPT_03=Sharp [nerve:easy]
- "What's behind it?" | [dice="composure:easy" win="Path_Intro_Clinical" lose="Fail_Intro_Clinical"]
- "We'll deal with it when it comes up."
	set {flags.CH_INTRO_01} = "OPT_INTRO_01_02"
	jump Path_Intro_Filed
- "You haven't looked very hard, or you haven't looked at all?" | [dice="nerve:easy" win="Path_Intro_Sharp" lose="Fail_Intro_Sharp"]

label Path_Intro_Clinical
set {flags.CH_INTRO_01} = "OPT_INTRO_01_01"
narrator: She looks up from the clipboard for the first time since she mentioned it.
bea: Storage, I think. That's what the building manager said when I asked. Storage.
player: [i]The pause before "storage" was one beat too long.[/i]
bea: Right. Where were we.
jump Merge_After_Door

label Fail_Intro_Clinical
set {flags.CH_INTRO_01} = "OPT_INTRO_01_01"
bea: Storage. Building manager confirmed it. Nothing interesting.
narrator: She's already back to the clipboard. You got the answer. It didn't feel like the answer.
jump Merge_After_Door

label Path_Intro_Filed
narrator: Bea's posture relaxes by a degree she probably thinks isn't visible.
bea: Good instinct. We have enough to deal with on this side of the door.
player: [i]She approved of that. Worth noting.[/i]
jump Merge_After_Door

label Path_Intro_Sharp
set {flags.CH_INTRO_01} = "OPT_INTRO_01_03"
narrator: A brief pause. She weighs you.
bea: At all. There. That's accurate.
narrator: The first real thing she's said since she walked in.
bea: I'll tell you if it becomes relevant.
jump Merge_After_Door

label Fail_Intro_Sharp
set {flags.CH_INTRO_01} = "OPT_INTRO_01_03"
narrator: She hears what you're doing. Decides not to confirm it.
bea: Haven't looked very hard. Like I said.
narrator: The clipboard comes back up. Subject closed.
jump Merge_After_Door

label Merge_After_Door
narrator: She moves on with the exact energy of someone who moves on for a living.
bea: Before we open the doors I need to register your profile. The admin software formats your formal correspondence — I need a few details.
bea: Gender identity, for the official records.
- "Male."
	set {game.player_gender} = "male"
	set {game.player_title} = "Mr."
- "Female."
	set {game.player_gender} = "female"
	set {game.player_title} = "Ms."
- "Non-binary."
	set {game.player_gender} = "nonbinary"
	set {game.player_title} = "Mx."
bea: First name.
[text_input text="First name:" var="game.player_first" placeholder="Adrian" default="Adrian"]
bea: Last name.
[text_input text="Last name:" var="game.player_last" placeholder="Cole" default="Cole"]
do GameState.build_player_name()
bea: Saved. You're officially in the system. Welcome to the building, {game.player_formal}.
player: [i]The building. Not the practice. Not the chair. The building.[/i]
narrator: She pulls three manila folders from the bottom of the box and sets them on the desk with the careful placement of someone presenting evidence.
bea: Your first intake pool. I filtered applications this morning.
player: How?
bea: I was carrying the full box up the stairs and tripped on the landing. These three slid the furthest under the fire door. I took that as a sign.
player: That's not a methodology.
bea: It's a working methodology. I read the files while I was down there. All three are exactly the kind of people who need this practice and will never admit it. They'll pay on time, they'll be difficult, and they'll be interesting. I have excellent instincts.
player: [i]She has, demonstrably, excellent instincts.[/i]
bea: I'm going to open the front entrance and forward the morning calls. You have forty minutes. Try not to rearrange the books — I have a system.
if {flags.CH_INTRO_01} == "OPT_INTRO_01_03":
	narrator: She pauses at the door. Doesn't look at the locked one.
	bea: I'll find out about the key. If I find anything worth telling you, I'll tell you.
	narrator: She leaves before you can answer.
else:
	narrator: She turns to go, steps neatly over the edge of the rug, and closes the door behind her with the deliberate care of someone who has made a point of it.
leave bea
do PatientManager.add_bea_relationship(1)
jump morning_menu/
